    {
      "id": "eaff801f-599f-4580-b20c-a2abfb842142",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 336,
      "shortId": "9R927",
      "priority": 3,
      "shortName": "paint-input-through-stack",
      "title": "Paint and route input through the layer stack",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "Today only hint visibility reads the stack. Draw layers in stack order and route input to the active or modal layer. The invariants must survive: no hardcoded z (z is tree position), buttons never declare a layer (they inherit it from their surface), the active context moves only for context surfaces — never for zoom, scroll or provider selection.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nClosed 2026-08-04 by a reconciliation pass — **the layer stack is laid out, painted and input-routed.**\n\n- **Layout, every frame:** `heca/src/chrome/mod.rs::layout_layers` runs `LayoutEngine::compute` on each visible layer root, so layer children get real measured bounds rather than hand-placed ones.\n- **Paint in stack order:** driven from the registry's ordering (`LayerBand` + `visible_roots_mut`), not from a hardcoded z — the invariant this task named.\n- **Input:** `dispatch_modal_pointer` (`chrome/mod.rs:1271`) delivers pointer events to the top modal layer and returns `true` so \"every caller stops there and nothing leaks to\" what is beneath. `top_modal` and `content_covered` answer which layer owns the context; keys reach an open overlay through the keymap and the widget's own `overlay_active` capture.\n- **Hints read the stack** through `collect_hint_targets(layer.root.as_ref())` (`:2185`).\n\nThe invariants held: z is tree position, buttons inherit their surface's layer rather than declaring one, and the active context moves only for context surfaces.\n\nLive proof beyond the tests: the command palette (P092/T393) mounts as an `Overlay`-band `OnDemand` layer, is laid out each frame, captures the keyboard while open, and occludes what is behind it.\n\n**Not re-verified visually as part of this pass** — it is exercised constantly by the palette, dropdowns and the confirm prompt, which Antonio drives regularly.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
